NAME
     zerocheck - fresh memory from the kernel must be zero

SYNOPSIS
     zerocheck [PAGES]

DESCRIPTION
     zerocheck takes PAGES pages with sbrk, reads every byte and requires
     it to be zero, then writes a pattern so that the pages are really its
     own, and says so. The kernel zeroes pages with cbo.zero at the
     cache-block size the machine is described with; a guest that believes
     a longer block than the hardware has leaves every other block
     unzeroed, and this is what shows it.

SEE ALSO
     memck(1)
